question:
What is printed in a multi-threaded environment?
```java
int x = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
  new Thread(() -> { x++; }).start();
}
Thread.sleep(100);
System.out.println(x);
```

What does this code do?
```java
synchronized void increment() {
  x++;
}
```

What is the output?
```java
Thread t1 = new Thread(() -> System.out.println("A"));
Thread t2 = new Thread(() -> System.out.println("B"));
t1.start();
t2.start();
```

What happens if you call start() twice on the same Thread?
```java
Thread t = new Thread(() -> System.out.println("Test"));
t.start();
t.start();
```

